WEBVTT

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:10.820
<i>It's making my chest tighten.</i>

00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:14.700
<i>What he does is  </i>not <i>boxing!</i>

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.820
<i>It’s not!</i>

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:21.450
It appears you’ve made up your mind.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.460
Yes.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:26.930
Very well.

00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.600
We’ll give them our reply.

00:00:28.600 --> 00:00:33.390
Your next title defense match will be against Sawamura Ryuuhei!

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:49.050
If it isn’t Ryuuhei!

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.050
Kawabe-sensei.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:57.100
I’m going to box in a Japanese title match.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.990
Th-The Japanese title?

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.600
Really? So you’re finally...

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:07.110
Thanks to you and the boxing gym you dragged me to, I’ll soon have a shot at the national title.

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:10.190
That's my boy! You're doing great!

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:12.170
I’ve been watching your matches.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.730
I believe they call you "The Flash."

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.960
"The Flash"?

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.000
Oh, you mean my counters?

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.000
I could easily win without them.

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.280
But with counters, you use your 
opponent’s strength against him.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.760
You know what that means, right?

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.500
You double the force of your hit.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.010
It also hurts them twice as much.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.340
That’s exactly how a math teacher would think.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:40.250
You get a different texture.

00:01:40.250 --> 00:01:42.770
They don’t feel like normal punches.

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:49.540
I get to chew on their flesh two times over.

00:01:50.190 --> 00:01:53.160
I really get the sensation that I’m bashing another man.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.150
Boxers are incredibly stupid.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.160
They actually come over...

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:03.370
and allow me to savor their sinews to my heart’s content.

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:10.800
This sport was practically made for me.

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.850
I love it when I get praised for laying someone flat on the ground.

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.280
Th-That can’t be right.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.060
You’re praised for your hard work and victories.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:26.090
You win at boxing by making
 your opponent lie at your feet.

00:02:26.090 --> 00:02:28.070
By drowning them in their own blood.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.570
I wonder how chewy the national champion’s flesh will be.

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:38.410
Will it be tough? Will it be tender?

00:02:48.010 --> 00:02:51.950
<i>I thought having you work diligently among strong men</i>

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:57.770
<i>would reform your spirit that was warped by the 
isolation that began after your mother abandoned you.</i>

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:00.180
<i>I really thought</i>

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:03.160
<i>that my friend’s boxing gym would help.</i>

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:08.300
<i>But that boy’s rare gift has caused him to become even more isolated.</i>

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:15.150
<i>What if I put him in exactly the wrong kind of environment</i>

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.890
<i>for a hungry mad dog?</i>

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.510
You’re really gonna fight him?

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.920
I've made my decision!

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:29.570
But what’s your actual plan?

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:33.720
You must have realized by now that your Dempsey Roll has a weakness.

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:34.560
What?

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:35.680
Weakness?

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:38.470
It ain’t good against counters.

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:44.600
Your clockwork horizontal weaving may get you your heavy blows.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:47.990
But that weaving is about as regular as a metronome.

00:03:47.990 --> 00:03:50.430
Anyone who gets that rhythm down and punches

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.730
will crush you like a melon.

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.320
He’ll feel the Dempsey Roll’s destructive force!

00:03:56.820 --> 00:04:02.140
Since today’s boxers rely on rhythm, speed, and 
counters, that move no longer amounts to much.

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:09.710
That being said, you still need to be a high-level technician who’s not afraid of the Dempsey.

00:04:10.540 --> 00:04:14.710
To my knowledge, the only guy in the nation who fits that description is Miyata.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:19.290
Sawamura-san said that my Dempsey was pathetic.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:21.840
I think he’s capable of pulling that counter.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.100
But that move is all I have.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.150
I want to take him down and 
beat him with my Dempsey Roll!

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:32.860
The kid finally found his swagger!

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.860
The odds are against you, you know.

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.410
If I want the odds to be in my favor, I’ll have to think of and refine...

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.990
an evolved Dempsey Roll!

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.220
Evolved?

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:44.870
Wow!

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:46.500
So how will it be evolved?

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:52.080
I haven’t thought that far.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.250
You haven’t thought of it yet?!

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.880
You were just blowing smoke up our asses?!

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:00.720
I-It’ll be fine, as long as I practice diligently.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.840
We have two outfighters who throw counters.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.240
Y-You mean us?

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:09.020
We’re in!

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.220
We’ll crush your Dempsey before Sawamura gets the chance!

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.320
All right, sparring time!

00:05:15.570 --> 00:05:18.020
Okay, I won’t pull any punches.

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:20.400
Sure, no kid gloves here either.

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:24.330
<i>I’m gunning for your Dempsey, so don’t feel bad when I crush it!</i>

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:26.790
Begin!

00:05:35.380 --> 00:05:37.550
He’s already doing his Dempsey!

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:42.640
<i>I see, it’s exactly like a metronome.</i>

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.890
<i>Tick, tock, tick, tock...</i>

00:05:45.890 --> 00:05:46.610
<i>Tick...</i>

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.380
<i>There!</i>

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.180
<i>Gotcha!</i>

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:58.190
What'd you step back for? Your timing was perfect!

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.250
Get outta there, you coward!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.930
You’re up, Itagaki!

00:06:02.890 --> 00:06:04.740
<i>I... I can’t!</i>

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:07.210
<i>I got Senpai’s timing down from way over here,</i>

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.950
<i>but my spine ran cold when 
Kimura-san was about to connect.</i>

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:12.880
Really? You’re gonna puss out too?

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.810
That's easy for you to say.

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.700
Then why don’t <i>you</i>  go up against him?

00:06:17.580 --> 00:06:20.890
It’s like sticking your hand inside a box of dynamite.

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:21.970
What?

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.020
Now do you get me, Ippo?

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.960
It may sound easy to match up your clockwork rhythm and punch you,

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:30.470
but you need technical skills and guts.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.230
If you don’t have both of them, you just can’t do it.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.190
You still need to create a new 
Dempsey Roll for Sawamura.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.490
But here’s the fatal rub:

00:06:40.490 --> 00:06:42.080
you have no way to train.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:46.020
You may think up a bunch of strategies,

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:50.240
but without proper training to fine-tune them, I don’t think they’ll work.

00:06:50.240 --> 00:06:53.120
They’ll fail just as hard as Takamura-san’s Look-Away—

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.710
So you need to think of a workaround,

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.500
or else you’ll lose.

00:07:00.240 --> 00:07:01.330
<i>Guts, huh?</i>

00:07:01.950 --> 00:07:04.610
<i>But what if guts were taken out of the equation?</i>

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.510
<i>If there was a way to do that...</i>

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:11.020
<i>Kimura-san didn’t hit him despite knowing the Dempsey’s weakness.</i>

00:07:11.970 --> 00:07:14.730
<i>He felt overwhelmed right after they started fighting.</i>

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.700
<i>If I can pin down what exactly made him pull back,</i>

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:21.770
<i>we can overcome that fear and use our counters.</i>

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:32.450
You aren’t putting your back into it!

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.090
Your thoughts are somewhere else.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:36.290
S-Sorry.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.190
I get what’s bothering you.

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:41.750
But it’ll take a lot of time to “evolve” anything.

00:07:41.750 --> 00:07:46.910
But I’m not going to stand here 
and tell you <i>not</i>  to think about it.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:49.050
Hell, you can fret all you want!

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:52.560
But, only when you’re pulling that thing behind you.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:08:00.310
Adding new twists and turns to your Dempsey Roll is going to require a whole lot out of your legs.

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:01.900
You will need strong legs

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:06.420
if you want to pull off your new Dempsey once that chance arrives.

00:08:06.420 --> 00:08:09.250
Now run, run, and run some more!

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:30.200
Our precious notes!

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.390
Th-Those are highly classified! Retrieve them now!

00:08:33.730 --> 00:08:34.640
Wait!

00:08:34.640 --> 00:08:36.060
Darn it!

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:39.810
What are these?

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:44.440
Oh, it’s just some reports we did on our own accord.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:45.570
Out of my way!

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:48.770
I-If you need our help...

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:52.570
...y-you can at least ask to borrow them.

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.880
Oh, quit your whining!

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:57.080
Right now I need all the help I can get!

00:08:58.180 --> 00:09:01.840
They made a detailed report on Aoki-san’s moves!

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:03.370
I’m actually impressed.

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:05.990
Any report on the Dempsey Roll?

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.830
I-In the back.

00:09:08.530 --> 00:09:09.260
There it is!

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:13.260
“The Dempsey Roll is...”

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:15.290
Where’s the rest?

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:16.610
Why's it left blank?!

00:09:16.610 --> 00:09:18.270
I-It was boring.

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:22.110
What do you mean "it’s boring"?! Hurry up and write the rest!

00:09:24.940 --> 00:09:28.650
I-If you’re going to complain, then give us back our notebooks.

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:31.660
D-Don’t put your hand beside my head like that!

00:09:33.610 --> 00:09:36.180
<i>Team Aoki actually scared me for a second.</i>

00:09:38.070 --> 00:09:38.910
<i>That’s right!</i>

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:40.830
Give them back!

00:09:42.710 --> 00:09:45.670
You guys come in handy once in a while!

00:09:48.650 --> 00:09:50.670
You discovered the secret behind the Dempsey?

00:09:50.670 --> 00:09:54.110
Yeah, namely why it’s so overwhelming,

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:58.060
and how to overcome our fear of it.

00:09:58.060 --> 00:09:58.890
Say that again?

00:09:59.560 --> 00:10:02.880
The keyword is “blind angle.”

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:07.650
That would mean outside the angle?

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:09.530
Precisely.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:12.880
The Dempsey Roll uses the recoil,

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:16.530
so from our point of view, it looks like he’s running left and right.

00:10:17.030 --> 00:10:21.290
After speeding from one blind spot to another, he lands a punch.

00:10:21.670 --> 00:10:25.790
He also arches his body as he punches, making it even harder to see where it’s coming from.

00:10:27.110 --> 00:10:32.380
That means Senpai’s incomparably destructive punches literally come out of nowhere.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:36.380
The fear created by that makes us less decisive.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:39.600
Even if we got the timing down, we’re less likely to throw a counter.

00:10:40.440 --> 00:10:43.600
So all we have to do is beat our fear of the blind spots!

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:45.380
B-But how?

00:10:45.380 --> 00:10:46.610
It’s simple.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:49.220
All you have to do is take a half step back.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:55.110
Once you increase your field of vision, the blind angle punches will disappear.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.680
So treat it like just another hook?

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.370
So Sawamura probably...

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:02.710
...figured it out as well.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:07.130
And I think that’s why he called
 the Dempsey Roll pathetic.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:09.000
Just another hook...

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:12.510
So that’s why it’s so damn easy to throw a counter.

00:11:13.460 --> 00:11:15.940
Let’s go now and help Senpai.

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:20.010
We might fail at first, but we’ll eventually land a counter.

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:21.960
You stay put!

00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:24.870
You still have your rookie tournament!

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:27.540
You have too much to lose if you make a mistake.

00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:34.950
So it’s up to me? I’m not sure I can!

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.520
Please, Kimura-san!

00:11:36.520 --> 00:11:37.730
Lay down your life, Kimura!

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:39.950
I don’t wanna!

00:11:42.720 --> 00:11:44.620
<i>I’m really getting impatient!</i>

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.750
<i>I know physical conditioning is important,</i>

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:49.500
<i>but I’m still worried to no end!</i>

00:11:50.000 --> 00:11:52.000
<i>I want to do some mock battles!</i>

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:58.300
No way.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:05.980
It can’t be.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:12.980
Vo...

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.030
<i>Here.</i>

00:12:16.650 --> 00:12:20.620
<i>I won’t need them once I return to my home country.</i>

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:22.660
<i>Makunouchi...</i>

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:27.070
<i>Farewell.</i>

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:30.720
I finally found you.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:32.720
Volg-san!

00:12:35.140 --> 00:12:36.660
What are you doing here?!

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:39.100
I don’t know what’s going on, but it’s been a while!

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:40.580
What brings you to Japan?

00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:42.430
Is it really you, Volg-san?

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:46.930
S-Slow down! I’m not <i>that</i>  fluent in Japanese!

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:49.310
Anyways, I’ve missed you!

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:51.460
You’re not here as a tourist, are you?

00:12:52.090 --> 00:12:53.190
So that means...

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:54.940
Yeah.

00:12:56.200 --> 00:12:58.190
I’m making a comeback.

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.850
<i>Is he the same guy I knew?</i>

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:03.200
<i>At least the sharp glint in his eyes hasn’t changed.</i>

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.550
I’m thinking of going to America,

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:09.870
so I’m here to retrieve what's mine.

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:11.630
You mean your gloves?

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:14.570
I still have them! I’ve been taking good care of them!

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:15.610
Thanks.

00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:20.550
Why are you so dirty?

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:25.600
I landed here two days ago, but
 I have no idea where you live.

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:29.290
Your country is warm enough for me to sleep anywhere, so...

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:30.870
You slept outside?

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:32.330
Come to my house!

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:35.480
Heck, you can stay as long as you want!

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.780
Dinner’s ready!

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:42.160
Oh, thank you very much.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:49.910
This is great! I love it!

00:13:51.490 --> 00:13:52.670
You're serving natto?

00:13:52.670 --> 00:13:54.290
Natto?

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:00.250
I’m sorry! Here’s some tea!

00:14:00.250 --> 00:14:01.670
I-I’m fine.

00:14:01.670 --> 00:14:03.470
What were you thinking, Mom?

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:05.630
I thought he never had it in Russia.

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:06.430
Gosh!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.360
I guess I shouldn’t have made it.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.160
Don't start him off with <i>that!</i>

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:10.980
I’m sorry!

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.550
<i>Mother.</i>

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:18.110
<i>I’ve had a hole in my heart since the day you left me.</i>

00:14:19.350 --> 00:14:21.950
<i>I am now leaving to fill that hole.</i>

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:24.570
<i>I’m returning to the ring.</i>

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:30.570
<i>There aren’t many rings that will take you.</i>

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:34.340
<i>Even your World Amateur Champion title won’t mean much.</i>

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.210
<i>You have a tough fight ahead of you.</i>

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:38.010
<i>I’m well aware of that.</i>

00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:41.940
<i>I’ll wager everything on my fists in the new land.</i>

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.220
<i>The land of freedom.</i>

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:46.340
<i>America?</i>

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:50.320
<i>First, I’m getting something I’ve entrusted to a friend.</i>

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:54.270
<i>I know my passion will rekindle
 once I meet him again.</i>

00:14:54.270 --> 00:14:57.460
<i>I have no misgivings; I only look forward.</i>

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:01.350
<i>I have nothing to dispose
 of or look back onto.</i>

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:11.200
Volg-san?

00:15:11.200 --> 00:15:13.390
What’s wrong? Are you okay?

00:15:13.390 --> 00:15:14.540
Uh, sorry.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:17.660
That reminds me, Makunouchi, I have a favor to ask.

00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:18.170
Sure thing!

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:21.940
The thing is I don’t know anybody in America.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.670
I don’t know where to go, either.

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:27.050
Y-You were going without a clear destination?

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:30.000
Could you tell me who to look up?

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:34.150
I’ll go ask my coach.

00:15:34.150 --> 00:15:35.510
I’m sure he’ll have an answer.

00:15:35.510 --> 00:15:39.100
Until then, you can stay here.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:40.690
I am most grateful!

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:48.440
Amazing!

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.530
You took down Sendou Takeshi with that infighting?

00:15:51.530 --> 00:15:55.160
Yeah, but here’s my last title defense.

00:15:59.630 --> 00:16:03.580
I guess you can call this match a test of endurance...

00:16:07.640 --> 00:16:09.270
Oh, sorry.

00:16:09.270 --> 00:16:11.490
I lost myself for a minute.

00:16:11.490 --> 00:16:14.960
I’m really impressed with that Dempsey Roll.

00:16:14.960 --> 00:16:18.900
I’ve been wondering what I would do against it.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:22.420
So what <i>would</i>  you do, Volg-san?

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.070
Huh?

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:37.960
That’s amazing!

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:40.420
You do this every night before going to bed?

00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:41.480
Yes.

00:16:41.480 --> 00:16:44.460
Someone once taught me how to split logs.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:46.160
Now I’m using this instead.

00:16:46.160 --> 00:16:49.340
It builds up my arm strength 
and stabilizes my lower body.

00:16:49.740 --> 00:16:53.090
I do 100 with each arm, then 100 using both arms.

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:54.470
That makes 300 each night.

00:16:54.470 --> 00:16:57.460
Three hundred? No wonder you’re strong.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:02.860
Actually, I also have a favor to ask you.

00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.610
Can you be my sparring partner?

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:11.660
You must have figured out the Dempsey Roll’s weakness.

00:17:13.710 --> 00:17:16.120
The Dempsey Roll is weak against counters.

00:17:16.740 --> 00:17:20.040
I’m going to fight an expert counterpuncher.

00:17:20.040 --> 00:17:22.110
But I’m unable to find a sparring partner—

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:23.850
I’m sorry, Makunouchi.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:29.340
I’m no longer the White Fang you once knew.

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:33.280
It’s been a long time since I’ve been in the ring.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:35.200
I won’t be of any use to you.

00:17:35.200 --> 00:17:37.060
N-Now wait!

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:39.020
You won’t be rusty at all!

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.880
You’ve become stronger.

00:17:41.880 --> 00:17:43.770
Really, really strong.

00:17:44.290 --> 00:17:48.440
Right now, I’m just a fangless wolf.

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:55.030
It will take time to rebuild my body and get back the feel I had for the ring.

00:17:55.500 --> 00:17:58.030
Your match will be over by then.

00:17:58.030 --> 00:17:58.830
I’m sorry.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.920
N-No, wait.

00:18:00.920 --> 00:18:04.110
I’m sorry I brought it up. Forget what I said.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:08.670
But Volg-san, don’t you dare say you’re fangless.

00:18:11.170 --> 00:18:13.070
You’re just hiding them.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:16.010
Your fangs are just as sharp as ever!

00:18:18.670 --> 00:18:19.750
Thanks.

00:18:23.550 --> 00:18:26.440
You’re the head coach of Karil, is this a joke?!

00:18:27.010 --> 00:18:31.690
I lent you a player whose punches can help you prepare for Makunouchi, and <i>this</i>  is how we’re treated?

00:18:32.110 --> 00:18:34.950
The bell rang. Hurry up and punch me.

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.580
But you’re turned to the side.

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:40.330
He said go! Just lay him out!

00:18:40.910 --> 00:18:42.080
<i>Mess around, will you?</i>

00:18:42.550 --> 00:18:45.170
<i>You won’t even see my goddamn punch!</i>

00:18:49.440 --> 00:18:50.800
That won’t do.

00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.030
You’re slow.

00:18:54.030 --> 00:18:57.800
Makunouchi’s headlong speed is three times faster than that!

00:18:58.600 --> 00:18:59.470
He kicked him!

00:18:59.470 --> 00:19:00.430
What are you doing?

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:03.940
Damn you! We’re never coming here again!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:05.610
Good.

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:07.440
He was a worthless sparring partner.

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:12.240
<i>I’m this close to expelling him for good, but wow!</i>

00:19:12.240 --> 00:19:17.600
<i>Not only did he  </i>not <i>flinch at a blind-angle 
shot that was similar to the Dempsey Roll,</i>

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:20.700
<i>he landed a perfectly-timed counterpunch to boot!</i>

00:19:21.110 --> 00:19:26.580
<i>The guy’s the worst scum imaginable, but he’s got the stuff of a top boxer.</i>

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:27.630
Coach.

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:29.340
Uh, what?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:31.720
I didn’t get enough.

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:33.340
I need more meat.

00:19:34.120 --> 00:19:37.840
Be sure to bring me more premium-
grade meat starting tomorrow.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:40.240
Make sure they’re speedy.

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:44.010
Get me pounds of flesh that’ll come at me fast and hard.

00:19:45.220 --> 00:19:47.640
You got it. I’ll get some for you.

00:19:48.310 --> 00:19:50.110
<i>He probably won’t get his fill.</i>

00:19:52.300 --> 00:19:57.480
<i>No matter how many he cuts down before the fight, they'll never satisfy his hunger.</i>

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:01.410
<i>He hones all his other senses with his writhing, insatiable hunger.</i>

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:06.540
<i>The mad dog will bare his fangs
 the day of the title match!</i>
